Title: Fix double-run anti-pattern in test_main.sh and test_check.sh
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: claude
Closed: done

--- log ---
2026-05-05T08:34Z claude created

2026-05-05T11:52Z claude closed — done
--- body ---
Two test files retained the double-run anti-pattern after the raid.

**`tests/test_main.sh` — all 5 cases (e.g., lines 15-16):**

```sh
out=$("$ERG" 2>&1 || true)          # run 1: capture output
if "$ERG" >/dev/null 2>&1; then     # run 2: check exit code
```

The exit code from run 1 is discarded; the output from run 2 is discarded.
On a non-deterministic binary (file read between calls, env differences)
the two runs can disagree. Replace with the single-run pattern.

**`tests/test_check.sh:160-166`** — the folder-closure warning test uses the
same structure: `out=$(cmd || true)` followed by `if cmd; then`.

**Fix:** `out=$(cmd 2>&1) && rc=0 || rc=$?`, then assert on both `$rc` and
`$out`. The fix is identical to what was applied in ticket 0044 to
`test_validate.sh`.
